# Landing page polish: favicon, OG image, GitHub link

**Severity:** Low
**Area:** static assets, `templates/landing.html`

## Problems

### 1. No favicon

`/favicon.ico` returns 404. No `<link rel="icon">` in any page's `<head>`. Browser tabs show the default blank document icon, which looks unfinished.

**Fix:** Create a simple favicon (the "m" wordmark or an Italian-themed icon) and add:
```html
<link rel="icon" href="/static/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
```

### 2. No Open Graph image

There's no `og:image` meta tag. When the URL is shared on social media, messaging apps, or Slack, the preview card has no image — just the title and description.

**Fix:** Create a 1200x630 OG image (can be a simple branded card with "Maestro" wordmark and tagline) and add the meta tag to the landing page.

### 3. GitHub footer link goes to github.com root

The footer contains `<a href="https://github.com">Source on GitHub</a>` — this links to the GitHub homepage, not the actual Maestro repository.

**Fix:** remove link

### 4. Reframe brand

Maestro's strengths:
- understand the student's life position/interests and build personalized plan around that
- CEFR accurate
- Grammar accurate

Focus more on these / surface them earlier

Remove:
- any mention of AI or open source

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Favicon displays in browser tabs
- [ ] Sharing the URL on social media shows a preview image
- [ ] "Source on GitHub" links to the actual repository
